Changes made by By Mel Ross (files carry a "Modified by By Mel Ross" or
"Added by By Mel Ross" note where they can hold a comment):
- Combined both projects into one skills folder and plugin (reel-editor sits in
  skills/3-editing/ beside edit-video); added skills/README.md, a guide to which
  skill to use when.
- reel-editor: gentle eased zooms by default, configurable in brand.json "zoom"
  (build_reel.py, auto_edit.py); configurable caption highlight shadow
  (build_reel.py); a Reel cover for every reel (new scripts/cover.py); delivery
  of a phone-size copy and the cover beside the full-quality file, optionally
  back to the footage folder (deliver.sh); a local review page for sessions
  without Artifact tools (new review/serve.mjs, references/review-local.md); a
  render option without "nice" (new scripts/render-nonice.sh, REEL_NO_NICE in
  render.sh and cut.py); ffmpeg 7+ filter-script flag (cut.py); HyperFrames
  pinned and telemetry off by default (render.sh, transcribe.py, tighten.py,
  qa.py, setup_engine.sh); doctor.sh finds HyperFrames skills kept outside the
  auto-loaded folder and checks for Chrome; SKILL.md, setup-interview.md and
  review.md updated to match.
- FavStash parts: plugin and package renamed to reel-studio; the remote FavStash
  connection is no longer added by the plugin (local only); validate-repo.mjs
  expects the reel-editor skill; AGENTS.md, INSTALL_FOR_AGENTS.md, README.md,
  CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md rewritten or updated;
  edit-video/SKILL.md points to reel-editor for talking-head clips. FavStash's
  logo, social preview and style preview images (from its maintainer's own reels)
  are not included.
- Added brand/: the By Mel Ross example brand (brand.example.json,
  brand.example.md, style-reference.md) with the Lora and Inter fonts, which are
  licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (license texts in brand/fonts/).

Changes made by By Mel Ross in Reel Studio 0.2.0 (November 2026). Modified files carry a
"Modified by By Mel Ross" or "Added by By Mel Ross" note; everything below is in
skills/3-editing/reel-editor unless a path says otherwise.
- Speaker cutout and layered graphics: new scripts/cutout.py and scripts/cutout_matte.swift (a
  person matte from Apple Vision on macOS, cleaned with ffmpeg, a transparent-video speaker
  layer, per-shot edge checks with a fallback to plain overlays); build_reel.py gains the card
  option "layer" (behind / front / both).
- Studio look: new scripts/enhance.py (denoise and sharpen on by default; exposure, colour, warmth and background blur available but off by default; before/after frame)
  called from cut.py, which also softens the background through cutout.py.
- Sound: new scripts/make_sfx.py (34 synthesised effects) and assets/sfx-manifest.json (source
  and license of all 40 effects, default level per effect); build_reel.py gains per-effect
  volume ("sfx_volume"), "sfx_events" and a stem-based audio path; setup_engine.sh generates
  the library; new scripts/mix_audio.py (voice / music / effects levels, music that dips under
  speech, two-pass loudness to -14 LUFS, true-peak limit, a measured report); render.sh calls it;
  new scripts/make_music_bed.py (an original, optional music bed).
- Checks and delivery: qa.py also checks true peak, clipping and the cover size; deliver.sh
  requires a 1080x1920 cover; doctor.sh checks the new needs.
- Docs and tests: SKILL.md, references/look-and-layers.md and references/sound-and-mix.md;
  README.md, brand/ examples (brand.example.json, brand.example.md), AGENTS.md and SECURITY.md
  updated; tests/reel-*.test.mjs added; scripts/validate-repo.mjs and .github/workflows/ci.yml
  extended; package.json and .claude-plugin/plugin.json version 0.2.0.
No third-party code, model or asset was added to this repository for these changes: the new
scripts use only the Python standard library, ffmpeg and (on macOS) Apple's Vision framework,
all installed separately (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

Changes made by By Mel Ross in Reel Studio 0.2.1 and 0.2.2 (November 2026), in skills/3-editing/reel-editor.
- 0.2.1: the studio look is natural by default: the colour grade (exposure, colour, warmth) and
  the background blur are off unless asked for (scripts/enhance.py, SKILL.md, docs, brand
  examples); denoise and sharpen stay on.
- 0.2.2, colour: iPhone HDR clips (HLG / PQ / BT.2020) are converted to standard colour up front
  with the HDR to SDR converter built into macOS (new scripts/hdr2sdr.py, called from cut.py;
  uses avconvert, part of macOS, nothing added to this repository). If the conversion is not
  possible the build says the colour is only approximate. The cut, the background-softened
  master and the full-quality and phone copies are labelled BT.709 (cut.py, cutout.py,
  deliver.sh); the background softening converts through RGB with exact rounding (cutout.py);
  render.sh and deliver.sh read the frame height robustly. SKILL.md and
  references/look-and-layers.md describe it; tests/reel-colour.test.mjs added; package.json and
  .claude-plugin/plugin.json version 0.2.2.
